00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.763
Because I'm gonna get him.

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:06.463
My client,

00:16:07.976 --> 00:16:10.559
the honorable Henry T. Fleming,

00:16:12.023 --> 00:16:14.690
should go right to fucking jail.

00:16:15.789 --> 00:16:19.640
The son of a bitch is guilty!
(court roaring)

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:24.050
- Okay, so Al Pacino has
had it with the system.

00:16:24.050 --> 00:16:28.720
He's the defense lawyer for this defendant

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:31.970
and he has had it with the defendant.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.820
And he says my client is guilty.

00:16:34.820 --> 00:16:36.760
A couple of problems with this.

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:41.100
Lawyers have a duty to their client.

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.210
Every state has rules of professional

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:46.170
conduct for the attorneys.

00:16:46.170 --> 00:16:49.990
And every defendant is
entitled to a zealous advocate.

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:54.990
Al Pacino has basically
given away all of his duties

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:58.170
to his client and basically conceded

00:16:58.170 --> 00:17:01.010
on his client's behalf
of the client's guilt.

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:04.410
Now that may present some big problems

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:07.143
for Al Pacino later on down the line.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:10.520
He's probably going to get disbarred.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.550
You are not allowed to take action

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:17.550
that is contrary to the
benefit of your client.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.900
And if he had problems with his client,

00:17:20.900 --> 00:17:24.300
the proper remedy would
be to ask the court

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:27.940
to remove him from the case and to give

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:31.970
his client time to find
other representation.

00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.250
It is not proper to admit to the

00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:37.843
jury that your client is guilty.

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.040
He'll likely get
disbarred for that action.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:47.460
So here Al Pacino has
violated many of the rules

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:50.580
of professional conduct
and he's likely to be

00:17:50.580 --> 00:17:53.610
disbarred pretty quickly
after this outburst in court.

00:17:53.610 --> 00:17:54.877
- He's guilty!

00:17:54.877 --> 00:17:56.069
- Your honor!
(court roaring)

00:17:56.069 --> 00:17:58.722
- Mr. Kirkland!
- That man is guilty!

00:17:58.722 --> 00:18:01.889
- That man there, that man is a slime!

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:04.970
He is a slime!
(many people yelling)

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.090
If he's allowed to go free,

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:10.270
