00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:12.123
- Mr. Kirkland, you are out of order!

00:18:12.123 --> 00:18:13.444
- You're out of order.

00:18:13.444 --> 00:18:14.497
You're out of order.

00:18:14.497 --> 00:18:16.961
The whole trial is out of order.

00:18:16.961 --> 00:18:19.320
They're out of order.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:24.320
- Yeah, so if you start
yelling at the judge like this

00:18:24.379 --> 00:18:27.320
and you violate the judge's instructions,

00:18:27.320 --> 00:18:30.500
which Al Pacino was
doing, you're very likely

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:32.790
to be held in contempt of court.

00:18:32.790 --> 00:18:36.610
The judge has enormous leeway to

00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:40.010
keep the order in his courtroom.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.650
And one of the ways that he can do that

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:44.160
is by sending attorneys to jail.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.980
So it's pretty rare, but
this is an instance where

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:53.470
really contempt is probably in order.

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:56.380
Al Pacino may go to jail here.

00:18:56.380 --> 00:18:59.600
And frankly, this
outburst is so prejudicial

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:03.380
to the client that,
frankly, I think the judge

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.790
would probably declare a mistrial,

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.610
which means that he would
disband the jury and they would

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:12.660
start the trial all over again
with a different jury pool.

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:16.019
That man, that's so crazy.
(gavel pounding)

00:19:16.019 --> 00:19:17.551
(many people yelling)
- We're in a court room!

00:19:17.551 --> 00:19:20.787
- Depraved man raped and
